  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2022) position from Midland Bank's own audited annual report \"MDB Financial Performance and Ratios: 5 Years Overview\", taken from the FY2023 report. SOLO / STANDALONE basis. Midland Bank was licensed in 2013, so FY2013 is the bank's first year of operation and this series covers its entire public history; there is no FY2011 or FY2012 to report. All figures are as reported by the bank; the source table prints total liabilities directly, so nothing on the balance sheet is derived. The row mapped to operating_profit is the bank's 'Profit before provision and tax' (labelled 'Profit before provision on loans and corporate tax' in some years), i.e. pre-provision operating profit. The FY2022 annual report extracts with no usable summary table (it is a scan or its embedded font defeats text extraction), so this year comes from the FY2023 report's comparative column. Classified loans are calculated as the reported NPL percentage applied to reported loans and advances, because the source table prints the ratio but not the absolute figure for most years. The provision charge for the year is calculated as profit before provision and tax minus profit after provision before tax; the source table's own provision row wraps across two lines and its label is lost in text extraction in several reports. The derivation reproduces the printed figure exactly where it is readable (FY2025: 2,702 - 1,110 = 1,592; FY2024: 2,114 - 1,125 = 989; FY2023: 1,743 - 1,277 = 466).",
